# ── CSP exceptions, and why they are still there ────────────────────────────
# script-src https://cdn.jsdelivr.net
#   tesseract.js (the on-device OCR fallback — the path where receipt images
#   never leave the phone) fetches its worker from
#   cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/tesseract.js@<version>/dist/worker.min.js. Dropping the
#   origin disables local OCR and forces every scan through Gemini, which is the
#   worse privacy outcome. Closing it properly means vendoring the worker and
#   the language data into /public and repointing workerPath/corePath/langPath —
#   a change that must be verified in a real browser, so it is tracked rather
#   than guessed at here.
# script-src blob:
#   Same dependency: the worker is instantiated from a blob URL.
# style-src 'unsafe-inline'
#   Tailwind's runtime style injection. Scripts are NOT inline-permitted, which
#   is the half that matters for XSS.
